  "thms": {
    "BookProof_ChapterBaryonAsymmetry_matter_satisfies_continuity": {
      "name": "BookProof.ChapterBaryonAsymmetry.matter_satisfies_continuity",
      "chapter": "ChapterBaryonAsymmetry",
      "file": "/home/leo/prove2me_workspace/Theorems/Thm_BookProof_ChapterBaryonAsymmetry_matter_satisfies_continuity.lean",
      "title": "The matter law satisfies the FRW continuity equation with `w = 0`: `a \u00b7 \u03c1_m'(a) + 3\u00b7(1 + 0)\u00b7\u03c1_m(a) = 0` for `a > 0`",
      "nl": "The matter law satisfies the FRW continuity equation with `w = 0`:\n`a \u00b7 \u03c1_m'(a) + 3\u00b7(1 + 0)\u00b7\u03c1_m(a) = 0` for `a > 0`. This fixes the dilution\nexponent `3`.\n\n\n\n**Formalization Note.** Lean 4 identifier: `BookProof.ChapterBaryonAsymmetry.matter_satisfies_continuity` (module `BookProof.BaryonAsymmetry`), line-linked source: `ChapterBaryonAsymmetry.lean` lines 67\u201381.",
      "source": "https://github.com/leonardopedro/timepiece/blob/61595bc/BookProof/ChapterBaryonAsymmetry.lean#L67-L81",
      "tags": [
        "timepiece",
        "qym",
        "baryon-asymmetry",
        "particle-physics"
      ]
    },
    "BookProof_ChapterBaryonAsymmetry_radiation_satisfies_continuity": {
      "name": "BookProof.ChapterBaryonAsymmetry.radiation_satisfies_continuity",
      "chapter": "ChapterBaryonAsymmetry",
      "file": "/home/leo/prove2me_workspace/Theorems/Thm_BookProof_ChapterBaryonAsymmetry_radiation_satisfies_continuity.lean",
      "title": "The radiation law satisfies the FRW continuity equation with `w = 1/3`: `a \u00b7 \u03c1_r'(a) + 3\u00b7(1 + 1/3)\u00b7\u03c1_r(a) = 0` for `a > 0`",
      "nl": "The radiation law satisfies the FRW continuity equation with `w = 1/3`:\n`a \u00b7 \u03c1_r'(a) + 3\u00b7(1 + 1/3)\u00b7\u03c1_r(a) = 0` for `a > 0`. This fixes the dilution\nexponent `4`.\n\n\n\n**Formalization Note.** Lean 4 identifier: `BookProof.ChapterBaryonAsymmetry.radiation_satisfies_continuity` (module `BookProof.BaryonAsymmetry`), line-linked source: `ChapterBaryonAsymmetry.lean` lines 83\u201397.",
      "source": "https://github.com/leonardopedro/timepiece/blob/61595bc/BookProof/ChapterBaryonAsymmetry.lean#L83-L97",
      "tags": [
        "timepiece",
        "qym",
        "baryon-asymmetry",
        "particle-physics"
      ]
    },
    "BookProof_ChapterBaryonAsymmetry_matterRadiationRatio_eq": {
      "name": "BookProof.ChapterBaryonAsymmetry.matterRadiationRatio_eq",
      "chapter": "ChapterBaryonAsymmetry",
      "file": "/home/leo/prove2me_workspace/Theorems/Thm_BookProof_ChapterBaryonAsymmetry_matterRadiationRatio_eq.lean",
      "title": "The book's \"proportional to the scale of the Universe\".** For a positive scale factor and nonzero present-day radiation density, the matter-to-radiation ratio equals `(\u03c1_{m,0}/\u03c1_{r,0}) \u00b7 a",
      "nl": "**The book's \"proportional to the scale of the Universe\".** For a positive\nscale factor and nonzero present-day radiation density, the matter-to-radiation\nratio equals `(\u03c1_{m,0}/\u03c1_{r,0}) \u00b7 a`.\n\n\n\n**Formalization Note.** Lean 4 identifier: `BookProof.ChapterBaryonAsymmetry.matterRadiationRatio_eq` (module `BookProof.BaryonAsymmetry`), line-linked source: `ChapterBaryonAsymmetry.lean` lines 99\u2013106.",
      "source": "https://github.com/leonardopedro/timepiece/blob/61595bc/BookProof/ChapterBaryonAsymmetry.lean#L99-L106",
      "tags": [
        "timepiece",
        "qym",
        "baryon-asymmetry",
        "particle-physics"
      ]
    },
    "BookProof_ChapterBaryonAsymmetry_matterRadiationRatio_strictMonoOn": {
      "name": "BookProof.ChapterBaryonAsymmetry.matterRadiationRatio_strictMonoOn",
      "chapter": "ChapterBaryonAsymmetry",
      "file": "/home/leo/prove2me_workspace/Theorems/Thm_BookProof_ChapterBaryonAsymmetry_matterRadiationRatio_strictMonoOn.lean",
      "title": "The matter-to-radiation ratio is strictly increasing in the scale factor (for positive present-day densities): expansion monotonically favours matter",
      "nl": "The matter-to-radiation ratio is strictly increasing in the scale factor\n(for positive present-day densities): expansion monotonically favours matter.\n\n\n\n**Formalization Note.** Lean 4 identifier: `BookProof.ChapterBaryonAsymmetry.matterRadiationRatio_strictMonoOn` (module `BookProof.BaryonAsymmetry`), line-linked source: `ChapterBaryonAsymmetry.lean` lines 108\u2013117.",
      "source": "https://github.com/leonardopedro/timepiece/blob/61595bc/BookProof/ChapterBaryonAsymmetry.lean#L108-L117",
      "tags": [
